<para id="RM0000005A600ZX" category="J" type-id="300N4" name-id="630WT-00" from="200612">
<dtccode/>
<dtcname>Tachometer Malfunction</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM0000005A600ZX_07" type-id="33" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___0000B4700000">
<name>Function Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<ptxt>The combination meter assembly receives the engine speed signal from the engine control computer via CAN communication. The combination meter assembly drives the tachometer based on the received engine speed signal.</ptxt>
<atten3>
<ptxt>The engine speed indication is greatly affected by the condition of the engine. This flowchart is designed for diagnosis on the assumption that there is no malfunction on the engine side. Before performing the inspection according to this flowchart, check that there is no malfunction in the engine. (see <xref label="Seep01" href="X39400000QQ017D"/>)</ptxt>
</atten3>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM0000005A600ZX_02" type-id="32" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___000005500000">
<name>Wiring Diagram</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="B162456J02" width="7.106578999in" height="2.775699831in"/>
</figure>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM0000005A600ZX_03" type-id="51" category="05" proc-id="RM0550J___0000B4800000">
<name>Inspection Procedure</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<atten3>
<ptxt>Before performing the inspection according to this flowchart, check that there is no malfunction in the engine. (see <xref label="Seep01" href="X39400000QQ017D"/>)</ptxt>
</atten3>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM0000005A600ZX_01" type-id="01" category="01">
<name>Procedure</name>
<testgrp id="RM0000005A600ZX_01_0001" proc-id="RM0550J___000005100000">
<testtitle>Perform TaSCAN Active Test (Combination Meter)</testtitle>
